=== fix commit msg
A model edit is saved right after it runs (the version callbacks, or the
document boundary for document-only actions). When that save threw, the
model was told one outcome and every later turn replayed another:

1. pump() called execute(), which set the record to Succeeded and
   notified subscribers.
2. AgentHost's subscriber stored the record and, in continue_after_tool,
   sent "succeeded" to the model and dropped the pending continuation.
3. The save then threw, and fail() rewrote the same record to Failed
   with local_save_failed and notified again.
4. The host stored the Failed record, but continue_after_tool had no
   continuation left, so the model was never told. Every later turn's
   history replayed the call as failed.

Fix, in the coordinator, which owns the outcome: the save is part of the
call's outcome. While a call's save is pending, notify() holds back its
terminal state; pump() runs the save, records local_save_failed if it
threw, and only then announces the outcome once. A failed save is what
the model should hear (its message tells the model not to repeat the
call and to tell the person the project is not saved), so the model
now receives "failed / local_save_failed" and the stored record says the
same. fail() now refuses (std::logic_error) to change a record that has
already been announced as finished, extending the "terminal records
never change" rule that cancel() already kept.

Tests:
- test_agent_bridge.cpp: a scripted provider makes a plate_layout call
  whose save after it throws. Asserts the tool result the model receives
  is failed/local_save_failed, the stored record says the same, and the
  next turn replays the same state and error. On HEAD the model received
  "succeeded" with no error while the record and the replay said
  "failed" (6 failed assertions).
- test_tool_coordinator.cpp: for both save paths (version callbacks and
  document boundary), exactly one terminal notification, Failed with
  local_save_failed, and the stored record equal to it. On HEAD both
  paths announced two terminal states.

agent_bridge_tests, every test except the 7 "MCP bridge ..." cases:
463 test cases, 16341 assertions, all pass (random order). The MCP
bridge cases fail and then hang in the harness destructor on this
machine with or without this change (checked by building HEAD's
coordinator and running them again), so they were left out.

